h specialty distributors, retailers, pool builders, and buying groups. Hayward Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1925 and is headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin P. Holleran | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $573K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue falling 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $116K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Hayward Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.5B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 48%.","The business throws off $227M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.69\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2172739541160619},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 8% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 21% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Gross margin tops the Industrials peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to HAYW Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Technical_Reactions_to_HAYW_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_112126032202_1795292522.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795292522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Analyzing Tecnoglass (NYSE:TGLS) & Hayward (NYSE:HAYW)","source":"thelincolnianon